{
  "suite": "shared/signed-delivery",
  "title": "Verifying an HMAC-signed delivery: the signed content, the key's spelling, rotation, replay",
  "contract": {
    "summary": "`verifyHmac` (TS) / `WebhookVerifier::verify` (PHP): the provider signs `payload` (a template over {id}, {timestamp} and {body}) with a key the secret spells (`secretEncoding` utf8 | base64, after `secretPrefix`), sends one or MORE signatures, and the delivery is accepted when any one matches inside the replay window.",
    "functions": {
      "verifyHmac": "verifyHmac({raw, signature: string | string[], secret, scheme, timestamp, now}) -> {ok: true} | {ok: false, reason}"
    },
    "reference": "authored",
    "referenceNote": "Two providers, checked against their own pages on 2026-09-15. Svix (Resend): signed content `${svix-id}.${svix-timestamp}.${body}`, HMAC-SHA256, base64 signature, secret `whsec_<base64>` DECODED to key bytes, header `svix-signature` a space-separated list of `v1,<sig>` that 'could be any number of signatures' of which yours must match one. Stripe: `${t}.${body}`, hex, text key, and while a secret is rolled 'Stripe generates one signature for each secret' and says compare against EACH. Hence: ANY match accepts; a first-only rule fails a roll for 24 hours and reads like a wrong secret. The replay window is the implementer's choice (Svix says so); 300 s here. Reasons are fixed strings. A runner builds `payload` from the template with the row's `id` and `timestamp`, passes `signatures` as the list (an empty list is no signature), and returns the verification result verbatim. HubSpot v3 (2026-11-01, developers.hubspot.com 'Validating requests'): signed content `${method}${uri}${body}${timestamp}`, HMAC-SHA256 under the app's client secret, base64, `X-HubSpot-Request-Timestamp` in MILLISECONDS with a 5-minute window, and the URI with only its QUERY portion percent-decoded for %3A %2F %3F %40 %21 %24 %27 %28 %29 %2A %2C %3B (never the leading ?, any #fragment dropped). 0015 is HubSpot's published worked example and reproduces from its inputs; 0017 is signed by that rule because no published example has a query. The runner passes the row's `method` and `url` as the request; the CORE normalises the uri, and the template only substitutes {method} {uri} {body} {timestamp}.",
    "implementations": [
      {
        "language": "node",
        "package": "@particle-academy/fancy-connector-core",
        "symbol": "verifyHmac from \"@particle-academy/fancy-connector-core\""
      },
      {
        "language": "php",
        "package": "particle-academy/fancy-connector-core",
        "symbol": "ParticleAcademyConnectorsWebhookVerifier::verify(raw, signature, secret, payload, algorithm, tolerance, timestamp, now, encoding, secretEncoding, secretPrefix)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "0001-svix-valid",
      "title": "Svix: id.timestamp.body, a whsec_ base64 key, a base64 signature — accepted",
      "input": {
        "scheme": {
          "algorithm": "SHA-256",
          "payload": "{id}.{timestamp}.{body}",
          "encoding": "base64",
          "tolerance": 300,
          "secretEncoding": "base64",
          "secretPrefix": "whsec_"
        },
        "id": "msg_p5jXN8AQM9LWM0D4loKWxJek",
        "timestamp": "1614265330",
        "now": 1614265340,
        "raw": "{\"type\":\"email.received\",\"data\":{\"email_id\":\"56761188-7520-42d8-8898-ff6fc54ce618\"}}",
        "signatures": [
          "U9MJNDKBCED9YuO9M3nQoR1gZcADfXpTeEPzXZ80mnI="
        ],
        "secret": "whsec_MfKQ9r8GKYqrTwjUPD8ILPZIo2LaLaSw"
      },
      "expected": {
        "ok": true
      }
    },
    {
